Craig wrote:

> Speaking of ''karni'', why does the note in my gi'uste say that the selkarni
> (contents of the journal) does not have to be subject matter?


Because a journal might contain fiction, and fiction doesn't really have
a "subject"; also a journal might be about miscellaneous subjects.
It's really the selection principle for the contents.  In the
limiting case, there is no principle at all, and the contents have
to be listed (as a set, presumably).

